0002 — classlink.rs + variance.rs: trait method binding as
`zend_do_traits_method_binding` / `zend_traits_copy_functions` /
`zend_add_trait_method` (requires 0001).

php-src binds the non-abstract trait methods before inheritance and the
abstract ones (requirements) after it:
 * a method the class declares itself wins over a trait method; two traits
   providing the same non-abstract method collide with "Trait method
   %s::%s has not been applied as %s::%s, because of collision with
   %s::%s" (the colliding side named by its trait and the name it was added
   under, e.g. an alias); the same code with the same visibility from two
   traits is not a conflict;
 * an abstract trait method that meets an existing method (own, from
   another trait, or inherited from the parent) is not added; instead the
   existing method is checked against it (`do_inheritance_check_on_method`
   with CHECK_PROTO but no visibility check: final, static/non-static and
   the signature, "Declaration of C::m(...) must be compatible with
   T::m(...)" where `self` in the trait signature resolves to the using
   class, at the line/file of the satisfying method). These checks need the
   VM, so build_class returns them in `LinkOut::trait_checks` and
   link_class runs them (`check_trait_abstract`); variance.rs gains
   `declaration_as` to show a method under its declaring scope's name while
   resolving self/parent in another scope;
 * a trait method that overrides a parent method inherits the parent's
   prototype scope (GH-14009);
 * each copy gets its own static variables (the op array is copied per
   using class);
 * `as` modifiers follow `alias->modifiers | (fn_flags & ~PPP)`, and
   making a non-final method `private final` through `as` raises the
   E_COMPILE_WARNING "Private methods cannot be final as they are never
   overridden by other classes";
 * zend_verify_abstract_class: an explicitly abstract class must still
   implement its private abstract methods ("Class %s must implement %d
   abstract method(s) (...)"), and the abstract check now runs after the
   method signature checks (as in zend_do_link_class), so an
   incompatible interface implementation reports the signature error.

Fixes Zend/tests/traits: abstract_method_1, abstract_method_3,
abstract_method_5, abstract_method_6, abstract_method_10, bug55355,
bug55424, bug60217b, bug60217c, bug60717, bug80055, gh12854, gh14009_001,
gh14009_002, gh14009_004, language010, language013, language014;
traits/bugs: abstract-methods02, abstract-methods04, abstract-methods05,
abstract-methods06; inheritance/argument_restriction_005;
type_declarations/variance/trait_success (24 tests).
Whole Zend/tests with 0001+0002: no new failures against phpt-baseline.txt.

